Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.98,0:00:06.14,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,My brother's...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.46,0:00:09.19,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,rather, Gilbert's mansion \Nhas been searched.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.19,0:00:11.94,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Documents connected to the \Nplot to murder Your Majesty
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.94,0:00:14.87,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,were found hidden in rooms underground.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.41,0:00:19.45,Default,Albert,0,0,0,,I see. So they've found \Nconcrete evidence.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.49,0:00:21.95,nameplate,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fade(272,477)\c&HEBEFEF&\3c&H564240&\pos(600,264)}Albert Ararat \N{\fs13}Crown Prince, Second Prince
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.45,0:00:21.76,Default,Albert,0,0,0,,That fool isn't even worthy \Nof comparison to a dog.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.93,0:00:25.41,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,And what will be done with him?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.41,0:00:28.81,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Premeditated murder of the \Nemperor is undeniably treason.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.81,0:00:32.74,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Under imperial law, there is no choice \Nbut to cut him in half at the waist.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.74,0:00:34.01,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.50,0:00:38.92,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,However, this case could be perceived \Nas merely attempted murder.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.69,0:00:41.89,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,And what would that entail?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.89,0:00:44.48,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,He isn't exempt from being cut in half,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.48,0:00:47.98,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,but he can still be granted the \Nminimum stay of execution.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.98,0:00:51.77,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,His sentence would then be carried out \Nonly when Your Majesty orders it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.77,0:00:54.46,Default,Albert,0,0,0,,Why complicate the matter like that?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.46,0:00:56.58,Default,Albert,0,0,0,,It's still execution by cutting in half.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.58,0:00:59.97,Default,Albert,0,0,0,,If he's to be executed anyway, what \Ndoes it matter when it's done?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.97,0:01:02.35,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,No, Noah has yet again proven wise.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.35,0:01:06.16,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,He has considered this from both \Nlegal and emotional perspectives.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.60,0:01:08.75,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,I appreciate you giving it such thought.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.18,0:01:12.67,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Gilbert is still the emperor's son.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.67,0:01:16.65,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Keeping in mind that he might love \Nhim too much to execute him,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.65,0:01:21.73,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,I gave him an option that would \Nessentially result in a life sentence.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.73,0:01:23.65,Default,Albert,0,0,0,,There is no need for hesitation.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.65,0:01:28.34,Default,Albert,0,0,0,,Those who attempted to kill you with \Npoison deserve immediate death.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.59,0:01:31.97,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Albert.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.38,0:01:35.49,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,I leave his execution in your hands. Go.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.49,0:01:36.43,Default,Albert,0,0,0,,Yes, sire.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.56,0:01:40.54,italics,Albert,0,0,0,,He really thought he could \Nget his hands on the crown.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.54,0:01:42.27,italics,Albert,0,0,0,,Pitiful.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.17,0:01:46.38,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Noah.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.91,0:01:49.06,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,You were right to tell me that.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.06,0:01:53.61,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,How brilliant of you to show such \Nconsideration in these circumstances.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.61,0:01:57.45,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,I feel your consideration has \Nbrought some degree of salvation.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.45,0:02:04.35,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Personally, I would like to transfer \Nownership of Gilbert's fief to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.35,0:02:05.34,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,You mustn't.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.34,0:02:06.42,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.96,0:02:10.77,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I informed you of Gilbert's \Nplot confidentially.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.40,0:02:13.59,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,If I were to receive his fief now,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.59,0:02:17.62,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,the other princes would start making \Nall kinds of reports anonymously
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.62,0:02:20.49,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,and sabotage each other in hopes \Nof earning the same reward.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.49,0:02:22.04,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Now, slow down.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.04,0:02:24.66,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,I only said I would {\i1}like{\i0} to do that.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.87,0:02:28.25,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,I don't mind my sons competing,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.25,0:02:31.89,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,but I can't have them trying \Nto sabotage each other.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.89,0:02:35.40,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,So I will not reward you this time.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.40,0:02:37.18,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I understand.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.60,0:02:40.73,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Instead, I will merely do \Nthat which is expected.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.73,0:02:43.75,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,You will soon be relocating \Nto your own fief.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.75,0:02:47.01,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,It's time to start thinking \Nabout your future wife.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.81,0:02:48.81,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Yes, sire.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.81,0:02:53.79,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,Engagement by age twelve is not \Nunusual in the imperial family.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.79,0:02:58.11,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,And a prince's first wife—his legal \Nwife, as opposed to a concubine—
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.11,0:03:00.39,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,is chosen for 100% political reasons,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.39,0:03:03.78,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,and must have standing \Nbefitting the role.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.25,0:03:10.04,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,For that reason, the prince himself has \Nessentially no say in who he marries.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.51,0:03:15.44,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,However, it is possible \Nfor fate to play a part.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.00,0:03:19.99,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,How about the granddaughter of \Nmy uncle, the Lightning Prince?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.99,0:03:21.53,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,The Lightning Prince...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.53,0:03:25.94,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,I believe he's been retired and out \Nof politics for many years already.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.28,0:03:31.40,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Divination has revealed that you and \Nshe will have a very clever child.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.40,0:03:34.56,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,I would only place the \Nprobability around 1%,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.56,0:03:38.73,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,but that child may even be \Nmore brilliant than you.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.73,0:03:43.57,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Nothing would make me happier than to \Ntake someone so remarkable as my wife.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.79,0:03:49.91,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,In that case, I will initiate \Nthe marriage negotiations.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.91,0:03:50.80,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Yes, sire.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.85,0:04:02.10,Default,Noizhill,0,0,0,,My, Prince Noah never ceases to amaze.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.22,0:04:08.38,Default,Noizhill,0,0,0,,He didn't even know the girl's \Nname or anything else about her.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.38,0:04:11.55,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,That's what it means to be a \Nprince—part of an imperial family.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.55,0:04:17.03,Default,Noizhill,0,0,0,,True, but it's natural for a young man \Nto take an interest in his future wife.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.03,0:04:19.49,Default,Noizhill,0,0,0,,To get past that at such a young age...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.49,0:04:21.83,Default,Noizhill,0,0,0,,What can it be called but amazing?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.35,0:04:24.65,Default,Noizhill,0,0,0,,"Choose a grandchild as your successor."
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.65,0:04:28.97,Default,Noizhill,0,0,0,,"A good grandchild guarantees \Nthree generations of prosperity."
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.97,0:04:31.75,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,It is indeed a good idea.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.75,0:04:36.06,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,But how likely is it, truly, that \Nmy grandchild could surpass me?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.06,0:04:40.59,Default,Noizhill,0,0,0,,At the moment, all that potential \Nlies with Prince Noah.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.59,0:04:44.10,Default,Noizhill,0,0,0,,If his brilliance passes \Ndown to his child...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.10,0:04:45.63,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.48,0:04:48.67,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,All we can do is hope, then.
Dialogue: 1,0:05:04.61,0:05:06.57,sign_generic,Title,0,0,0,,{\fade(109,0)\c&H4F7C81&\bord0\fnTimes New Roman\b1\fs10\pos(320,142.5)}Born Blessed, So I'll Obtain Ultimate Power
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.61,0:05:06.57,sign_generic,Title,0,0,0,,{\fade(109,0)\p1\bord2\c&H291505&\alpha&H255&\3c&H2986A5&\fscx87\pos(311,141.167)}m 0 0 l 235 0 l 225 8 l 235 15 l 18 15 l 30 8 l 18 0
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.42,0:06:23.40,Default,Don,0,0,0,,I am resigned to my fate.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.73,0:06:28.30,Default,Don,0,0,0,,I make no excuses for my betrayal of \NPrince Gilbert, my former master.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.30,0:06:30.47,Default,Don,0,0,0,,Please, at least, make it quick.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.47,0:06:33.71,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Don't be so hasty. Who said any of that?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.71,0:06:35.29,Default,Don,0,0,0,,B-But...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.29,0:06:38.16,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,People are treasures.\NI don't kill them on a whim.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.58,0:06:43.05,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,And imperial law says an indicted man\Nwho exposes treason is to be acquitted.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.44,0:06:44.51,Default,Don,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.73,0:06:47.51,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I called you here for a few reasons.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.96,0:06:50.58,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,First, Gilbert has been executed,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.58,0:06:53.08,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,and all power he possessed has collapsed.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.08,0:06:57.50,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,So there's no longer any need for you to \Nchange your name and leave the capital.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.50,0:06:59.40,Default,Don,0,0,0,,O-Oh...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.83,0:07:05.35,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,And exposing treason is worth \Na reward of up to 1,000 rean.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.35,0:07:09.41,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I'll add another zero to \Nthat out of my own pocket.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.41,0:07:12.89,Default,Don,0,0,0,,What? Wh-Why would you \Ngive me so much money?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.89,0:07:15.58,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Because you saved my father's life.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.32,0:07:20.38,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I could return you to the Department\Nof the Imperial Household
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.38,0:07:23.17,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,as a member of my household,\Nbut I want to hear what {\i1}you{\i0} want.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.44,0:07:25.62,Default,Don,0,0,0,,Incredible...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.43,0:07:29.38,Default,Don,0,0,0,,You are my master for life.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.81,0:07:33.05,Default,Don,0,0,0,,No matter where I go, I will \Nobey your every command.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.36,0:07:34.48,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.83,0:07:38.72,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Zoey, you heard that, yes?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.72,0:07:40.31,Default,Zoey,0,0,0,,Y-Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.31,0:07:43.13,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Your mother is no longer in danger.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.13,0:07:45.06,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Tell her she can rest at ease.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.06,0:07:48.70,Default,Zoey,0,0,0,,Master, you even\Nremembered my mother...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.27,0:07:50.96,Default,Zoey,0,0,0,,Thank you so much.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.75,0:08:02.26,top,Cheryl,0,0,0,,This is the capital of \Na nation of warriors,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.03,0:08:02.26,Default,Gigi,0,0,0,,Master?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.26,0:08:06.60,top,Cheryl,0,0,0,,but I have yet to see anyone \Nwho looks like a warrior!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.31,0:08:06.60,Default,Gigi,0,0,0,,It sounds like something interesting \Nis going on over there.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.50,0:08:13.36,Default,Cheryl,0,0,0,,Well? Is there anyone who \Nwishes to challenge me?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.87,0:08:16.54,Default,Cheryl,0,0,0,,All you need to do is fight me and win.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.54,0:08:18.47,Default,Cheryl,0,0,0,,The entry fee is three rean.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.47,0:08:20.62,Default,Onlooker1,0,0,0,,And what do we get if we win?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.62,0:08:21.96,Default,Cheryl,0,0,0,,Me.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.96,0:08:25.79,Default,Cheryl,0,0,0,,I'll be your wife, your mistress, your \Nservant, whatever you tell me to be.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.19,0:08:28.20,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,In imperial law, illegal \Nslave-trading is defined as
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.20,0:08:30.71,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,"the buying and selling of other people."
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.32,0:08:34.37,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Selling oneself doesn't \Nviolate that, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.37,0:08:36.49,Default,Challenger1,0,0,0,,So I just gotta defeat you, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.49,0:08:39.12,Default,Cheryl,0,0,0,,Yeah, but it has to be one-on-one.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.12,0:08:41.03,Default,Challenger1,0,0,0,,That was my intention from the start.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.03,0:08:45.00,Default,Onlooker1,0,0,0,,Otherwise, even if I won, \NI'd have to share you!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.12,0:08:52.45,Default,Cheryl,0,0,0,,Three rean.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.45,0:08:53.41,Default,Challenger1,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.75,0:08:56.02,Default,Challenger1,0,0,0,,You didn't pay the entry fee.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.02,0:08:57.71,Default,Onlooker1,0,0,0,,Oof, that's embarrassing!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.71,0:09:00.21,Default,Onlooker2,0,0,0,,He challenged her without paying \Nand lost within seconds!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.21,0:09:01.36,Default,Challenger1,0,0,0,,Damn it!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.36,0:09:03.69,Default,Challenger1,0,0,0,,Okay, who's next?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.97,0:09:05.13,Default,Man1,0,0,0,,That'll be me!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:05.13,0:09:06.33,Default,Man2,0,0,0,,Then I'm after him!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.33,0:09:07.64,Default,Man3,0,0,0,,And I'm after him!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.48,0:09:16.78,Default,Gigi,0,0,0,,Wow! That's fifteen challengers down!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.29,0:09:19.74,Default,Cheryl,0,0,0,,Okay, who's next?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.74,0:09:21.79,Default,Man4,0,0,0,,Y-You do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.79,0:09:22.91,Default,Man5,0,0,0,,No way, man.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.20,0:09:26.49,Default,Chad,0,0,0,,I'll do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.97,0:09:28.42,Default,Cheryl,0,0,0,,Hey, you need to pay.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.72,0:09:30.78,Default,Chad,0,0,0,,There'll be no need for that.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.78,0:09:33.54,Default,Chad,0,0,0,,'Cause I'm gonna be the one... to win!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.35,0:09:44.96,Default,Onlookers,0,0,0,,Wh-What just happened?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.96,0:09:46.43,Default,Onlookers,0,0,0,,He beat her that easily...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.29,0:09:49.46,Default,Chad,0,0,0,,Now you belong to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.46,0:09:50.46,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Hold it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.45,0:09:54.31,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,That has to be against the rules.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.31,0:09:55.39,Default,Chad,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.39,0:09:58.23,Default,Chad,0,0,0,,What's your deal, kid? \NQuit griping about—
Dialogue: 0,0:09:58.23,0:10:00.26,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,You used some sort of \Nnumbing drug, didn't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.70,0:10:03.89,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,If you made someone else \Ndo that, it's two-on-one.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.71,0:10:06.89,Default,Chad,0,0,0,,Wh-What are you talking about?!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.89,0:10:08.55,Default,Chad,0,0,0,,Where's your proof that—
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.83,0:10:15.12,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Found him.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.12,0:10:17.35,Default,Chad,0,0,0,,I-I don't know that guy!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.35,0:10:20.67,Default,Onlooker1,0,0,0,,Don't lie, Chad!\NThat's your henchman, Rob!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.67,0:10:22.98,Default,Onlooker2,0,0,0,,You were just drinking with \Nhim at my bar yesterday!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.98,0:10:25.48,Default,Onlooker3,0,0,0,,Put the girl down, you coward!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.31,0:10:31.02,Default,Chad,0,0,0,,Little brat! You'll pay for butting in!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:43.06,0:10:44.89,Default,Onlooker2,0,0,0,,Just look at him now!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.89,0:10:46.54,Default,Onlooker3,0,0,0,,That kid's incredible!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.54,0:10:48.38,Default,Onlooker3,0,0,0,,He was so fast, I didn't see a thing!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.38,0:10:49.73,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Do you want to continue?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.53,0:10:53.61,Default,Chad,0,0,0,,Y-Y-Y...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.61,0:10:56.03,Default,Chad,0,0,0,,You're gonna pay for this!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.18,0:10:58.51,top,Rob,0,0,0,,W-Wait for me, Chad!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:03.62,0:11:05.20,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Are you awake now?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.12,0:11:09.09,Default,Cheryl,0,0,0,,Who are... you?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.09,0:11:12.20,Default,Proprietress,0,0,0,,You ought to be grateful to this boy.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.20,0:11:14.94,Default,Proprietress,0,0,0,,He saved your life, you know.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.94,0:11:16.26,Default,Cheryl,0,0,0,,He did?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.26,0:11:18.21,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,How much do you remember?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.21,0:11:22.25,Default,Cheryl,0,0,0,,I remember... fighting with some creep...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.25,0:11:24.79,Default,Cheryl,0,0,0,,and suddenly, my legs \Nwouldn't move anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.79,0:11:26.87,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,He had his friend attack you.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.39,0:11:28.55,Default,Cheryl,0,0,0,,That coward!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.55,0:11:31.71,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I don't deny that, but you \Nwere also too careless.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.62,0:11:35.30,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Why were you out there \Ndoing that, anyway?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.30,0:11:36.96,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Tell me.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.56,0:11:41.20,Default,Cheryl,0,0,0,,I ran out of money...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.70,0:11:45.09,Default,Cheryl,0,0,0,,I came here for the \Nknight selection exam,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.09,0:11:47.19,Default,Cheryl,0,0,0,,but I didn't make the cut.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.19,0:11:50.24,Default,Cheryl,0,0,0,,I don't even have the money \Nto go home... so I...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.24,0:11:52.40,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Wait. That doesn't make sense.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.40,0:11:54.34,Default,Cheryl,0,0,0,,What doesn't make sense?!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.34,0:11:56.75,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I saw your skills back there.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.75,0:11:58.37,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,You couldn't have failed.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.81,0:12:01.65,Default,Cheryl,0,0,0,,I didn't agree with it either, \Nso I looked into it.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.04,0:12:06.47,Default,Cheryl,0,0,0,,But then this year's head judge, \Nthe Tenth Prince, summoned me
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.47,0:12:09.17,Default,Cheryl,0,0,0,,and said he'd be willing \Nto let me progress...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.26,0:12:12.34,Default,Cheryl,0,0,0,,but in return, as a woman, I'd have to...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.34,0:12:15.11,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Okay, that's enough. I understand.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.71,0:12:18.73,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,That particular brother \Nis the type to say that.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.24,0:12:20.99,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Do you still want to be a knight?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.99,0:12:22.11,Default,Cheryl,0,0,0,,Of course!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.11,0:12:25.81,Default,Cheryl,0,0,0,,Even if it takes years, I'll \Nbecome a knight on my own merit!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.16,0:12:28.34,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Then you don't need to return home.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.19,0:12:30.35,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Here's 100 rean.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.69,0:12:34.06,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,It should be enough to live on until \Nthe next knight selection exam.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.06,0:12:34.83,Default,Cheryl,0,0,0,,Wha...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.74,0:12:38.68,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Gigi, see to her living arrangements.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.68,0:12:39.98,Default,Gigi,0,0,0,,Understood.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.98,0:12:43.43,Default,Cheryl,0,0,0,,Wh-What is this about? Why do all this?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.43,0:12:45.50,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Because I like you.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.93,0:12:49.32,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,You want recognition not for your \Nwomanhood, but based on merit.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.62,0:12:51.49,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I like that sort of person.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.89,0:12:55.09,Default,Cheryl,0,0,0,,Who are you? You're not just some kid.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.71,0:12:56.88,Default,Chad,0,0,0,,There he is!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:58.28,0:12:59.20,Default,Chad,0,0,0,,That's the brat!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.55,0:13:02.46,Default,Chad,0,0,0,,You had some nerve \Nhumiliating me back there!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.46,0:13:04.42,Default,Chad,0,0,0,,Boss, you tell 'em, too!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:04.42,0:13:05.61,Default,Cheryl,0,0,0,,You're—
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.61,0:13:06.85,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Stay back.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.29,0:13:11.40,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Oh?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.74,0:13:13.68,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,You want to do the honors?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.68,0:13:16.39,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Then I'll link you with \Nmy armor ring and...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.58,0:13:19.69,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,There.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.25,0:13:26.17,Default,Punk1,0,0,0,,Wh-What the hell?!\NHis fists are on fire!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.17,0:13:28.36,Default,Punk2,0,0,0,,I've never seen anything \Nlike that before!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.36,0:13:30.89,Default,Chad,0,0,0,,Hey! No chickening out! Get him!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.78,0:13:42.09,Default,Chad,0,0,0,,R-Rob!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.16,0:13:59.85,Default,Cheryl,0,0,0,,Wow... No wasted movements at all...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.85,0:14:01.55,Default,Cheryl,0,0,0,,He's {\i1}that{\i0} strong?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.25,0:14:04.72,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,You're not going to fight?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:04.72,0:14:06.99,Default,Cheryl,0,0,0,,That's the Tenth Prince's knight!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:07.81,0:14:10.54,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Ah. I get it now.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:11.78,0:14:15.93,Default,Knight,0,0,0,,P-P-P-Please forgive me,\NThirteenth Prince!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.57,0:14:19.89,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,I get that they were paid \Nunder the table to do this,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.89,0:14:21.75,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,but once they knew who I was,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.75,0:14:24.63,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,they thought they could avoid \Ngetting caught if they kept quiet.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.98,0:14:27.92,Default,Cheryl,0,0,0,,Thirteenth... Prince?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.45,0:14:32.02,Default,Cheryl,0,0,0,,You're the Wise Prince,\Nthe minister-prince of justice?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.02,0:14:34.29,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Yes. Noah Ararat.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.16,0:14:37.28,italics,Cheryl,0,0,0,,The real deal?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.28,0:14:41.15,italics,Cheryl,0,0,0,,Well, that would explain \Neverything that's happened.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.41,0:14:43.23,italics,Cheryl,0,0,0,,He's a prince and a minister,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.23,0:14:45.22,italics,Cheryl,0,0,0,,but he doesn't flaunt his status at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.87,0:14:48.40,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I'll let you handle their punishment.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.10,0:14:51.59,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Did you try to attack me?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.12,0:14:56.02,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I'll let you off the hook \Njust this once. Take them.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.02,0:14:57.80,Default,Knight,0,0,0,,Y-Yes, Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.44,0:15:00.03,Default,Knight,0,0,0,,Come on, get moving!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.43,0:15:07.18,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,What an impressive boy you are.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.18,0:15:09.75,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,Your looks and skills are both top-notch.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.39,0:15:12.01,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Who is he?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.01,0:15:15.79,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,I don't often see such \Nremarkable young men.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.18,0:15:18.89,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,The Golden Gourd?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.94,0:15:23.15,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,I just recently learned \Nabout that and its owner!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.14,0:15:27.97,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,It is an honor to meet you,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.75,0:15:31.69,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Your Imperial Highness \Nthe Lightning Prince.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.69,0:15:34.48,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,Ah, so you know who I am.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.48,0:15:36.72,Default,Onlooker1,0,0,0,,Is that guy a prince, too?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.72,0:15:39.11,Default,Onlooker2,0,0,0,,I feel like I've heard \Nthat name before...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.38,0:15:43.03,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,The Lightning Prince, Indra Ararat.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.34,0:15:47.97,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,A few decades ago, when the current \Nemperor assumed the throne,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.41,0:15:52.40,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,he stood in the center of \Npower as the Prince Regent.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.40,0:15:56.68,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,The empire was in chaos because \Nthe emperor was so young,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.40,0:16:00.27,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,but he proved capable enough \Nto take control of it all.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.96,0:16:03.82,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Five years later, the Prince \NRegent stepped aside,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.82,0:16:06.37,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,choosing to retire to his \Nfief without argument...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.23,0:16:14.41,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\c&HF6F6F6&\3c&H0FAFD8&\fnTimes New Roman\fs32\b1\blur2\t(0,513,\3c&H1098F2&)\t(513,1026,\3c&H075FC7&)\t(1026,1539,\3c&H0FAFD8&)\t(1539,2052,\3c&H1098F2&)\t(2052,2565,\3c&H075FC7&)\t(2565,3078,\3c&H0FAFD8&)\t(3078,3591,\3c&H1098F2&)\t(3591,4104,\3c&H075FC7&)\t(4104,4617,\3c&H0FAFD8&)\t(4617,5130,\3c&H1098F2&)\t(5130,5643,\3c&H075FC7&)\t(5643,6156,\3c&H0FAFD8&)\t(6156,6669,\3c&H1098F2&)\t(6669,7180,\3c&H075FC7&)}Lightning
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.70,0:16:11.15,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,and he earned the title of \N"Lightning" for his role
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.15,0:16:13.71,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,in ushering in the emperor's \Nnew administration.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.73,0:16:19.07,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,And now such a great man suddenly \Nshows up in the capital?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.46,0:16:21.67,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,Come over here and sit down.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:21.67,0:16:23.18,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Thank you, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.29,0:16:28.15,sign_generic,EPTitle,0,0,0,,{\fnTimes New Roman\bord0\b1\fade(484,706)\c&H00070B&\pos(320, 205)}Episode 10
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.29,0:16:28.15,sign_generic,EPTitle,0,0,0,,{\fnTimes New Roman\bord0\b1\fade(484,706)\c&H00070B&\pos(320, 225)}Lightning Prince and Wise Prince
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.55,0:16:31.51,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,Since you know who I am...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.51,0:16:35.68,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,I assume the emperor has \Nalready spoken to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.68,0:16:37.90,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Yes, he spoke to me himself.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.90,0:16:42.13,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,I see, I see. Then you also \Nknow why I've come here.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:43.20,0:16:45.35,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,To evaluate me?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:45.69,0:16:49.34,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,The emperor chose you \Nbecause he trusts you,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.34,0:16:52.32,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,so there's really no need for \Nme to verify anything...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.32,0:16:55.68,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,but this does affect the life \Nof my granddaughter, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.68,0:17:00.11,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,The way he speaks would \Nmake an inspector furious.
Dialogue: 1,0:17:00.12,0:17:06.29,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs18\fnTimes New Roman\bord0\b1\c&H465156&\pos(172,21.332)}Emperor
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.12,0:17:06.29,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\an8\bord2\shad2\blur1\p1\fscy220\alpha&H50&\c&HE9EBEB&\3c&H97C1D0&\shad0\pos(172,15.333)}m 0 0 l 75 0 75 15 0 15
Dialogue: 1,0:17:00.12,0:17:06.29,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs10\fnTimes New Roman\bord0\b1\c&H465156&\pos(258,70)}Uncle \N(Lightning Prince) \N{\fs12}Indra
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.12,0:17:06.29,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\an8\bord2\shad2\blur1\p1\fscy220\alpha&H50&\c&HE9EBEB&\3c&H97C1D0&\shad0\pos(259,69)}m 0 0 l 75 0 75 15 0 15
Dialogue: 1,0:17:00.12,0:17:06.29,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs10\fnTimes New Roman\bord0\b1\c&H465156&\pos(172,75)}Brother \N{\fs12}Graeme
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.12,0:17:06.29,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\an8\bord2\shad2\blur1\p1\fscy220\alpha&H50&\c&HE9EBEB&\3c&H97C1D0&\shad0\pos(172,69)}m 0 0 l 75 0 75 15 0 15
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.41,0:17:03.17,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Although he is the emperor's \Nuncle, he remains his subject.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.10,0:17:06.29,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fade(2255,0)\an8\bord2\shad2\blur1\p1\fscy220\alpha&H50&\c&HE9EBEB&\3c&H97C1D0&\shad0\pos(259,110)}m 0 0 l 75 0 75 15 0 15
Dialogue: 1,0:17:01.89,0:17:06.29,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fade(1423,0)\fs10\fnTimes New Roman\bord0\b1\c&H465156&\pos(258,115)}Fourth Prince \N{\fs12}Henry
Dialogue: 1,0:17:01.99,0:17:06.29,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fade(1423,0)\fs10\fnTimes New Roman\bord0\b1\c&H465156&\pos(172,115)}Third Prince \N{\fs12}Kiro
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.99,0:17:06.29,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fade(2255,0)\an8\bord2\shad2\blur1\p1\fscy220\alpha&H50&\c&HE9EBEB&\3c&H97C1D0&\shad0\pos(172,110)}m 0 0 l 75 0 75 15 0 15
Dialogue: 1,0:17:02.70,0:17:06.29,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fnTimes New Roman\b1\bord1.5\fs15\fade(530,0)\c&H2A3938&\3c&H8F908E&\pos(172,50)}(Subjects)
Dialogue: 1,0:17:02.75,0:17:06.29,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fade(2357,0)\fs10\fnTimes New Roman\bord0\b1\c&H465156&\pos(85,75)}First Prince \N{\fs12}Gilbert
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.75,0:17:06.29,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fade(2357,0)\an8\bord2\shad2\blur1\p1\fscy220\alpha&H50&\c&HE9EBEB&\3c&H97C1D0&\shad0\pos(85,69)}m 0 0 l 75 0 75 15 0 15
Dialogue: 1,0:17:02.75,0:17:06.29,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fade(2357,0)\fs10\fnTimes New Roman\bord0\b1\c&H465156&\pos(85,110)}Crown Prince,\NSecond Prince \N{\fs12}Albert
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.75,0:17:06.29,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fade(2375,0)\an8\bord2\shad2\blur1\p1\fscy220\alpha&H50&\c&HE9EBEB&\3c&H97C1D0&\shad0\pos(85,110)}m 0 0 l 75 0 75 15 0 15
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.17,0:17:06.28,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,For him to simply address him as "the \Nemperor" is extremely disrespectful.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.46,0:17:11.67,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,But... well, I don't think he'd even \Ncare if I called him out on it.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.67,0:17:13.94,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,I don't think my father would \Nfind fault with him, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:14.47,0:17:17.00,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,That's just how this man is.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.00,0:17:21.34,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,What will you do if I don't \Nmeasure up to your standards?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.60,0:17:25.22,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,I just won't let you \Nmarry her, that's all.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.22,0:17:27.07,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,But this was an imperial \Ncommand, was it not?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.07,0:17:28.68,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,That doesn't mean a thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:28.68,0:17:32.98,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,Sure, if it were any other order from \Nthe emperor, I'd obey at any cost.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.98,0:17:36.62,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,But this is my granddaughter, you know.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.28,0:17:40.51,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,This is my precious little \Ngranddaughter we're talking about.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.51,0:17:43.99,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,That means it's not political.\NIt's personal.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.99,0:17:48.63,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,And the one who gave the order is my \Nnephew, the boy I once bounced on my knee.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.12,0:17:52.77,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,If he's wrong, I'll smack him upside the \Nhead if that's what it takes to stop him.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:52.77,0:17:55.79,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,I see. He's an interesting man.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:56.16,0:17:59.05,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,I don't think he has any \Ndesire to gain power.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.05,0:18:01.59,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,That's why he doesn't get \Nrebuked for being rude.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.59,0:18:03.03,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,In fact, this is preferred.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.40,0:18:05.60,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,So... do I pass?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.53,0:18:09.05,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,That's what I'm about to find out.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.16,0:18:14.56,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,What is this? It feels like \Nsomething's crushing me...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.56,0:18:17.69,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,It's just like what I make Leviathan do!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.15,0:18:19.44,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,The menace!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.14,0:18:22.37,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,In that case...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.37,0:18:24.33,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,I'll push back!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:24.33,0:18:25.66,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,Oh?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:26.41,0:18:28.63,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Good! Now, with one blow...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.93,0:18:30.82,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,No, I shouldn't.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.11,0:18:35.71,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,He's my great-uncle and, potentially, \Nmy future grandfather-in-law.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.71,0:18:38.46,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,I shouldn't injure him in public.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.46,0:18:42.80,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,I'll control this so I \Nneither win nor lose.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.29,0:18:48.93,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,Impressive, boy! I admit defeat!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.93,0:18:51.66,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Um... I thought it was a draw...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.66,0:18:52.93,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,No, blockhead.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:52.93,0:18:57.40,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,You read my technique perfectly \Nand {\i1}made{\i0} it a draw.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.40,0:18:59.52,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,Your mindfulness did me in.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.42,0:19:04.49,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,He calls it mindfulness,\Nbut he gave it away himself.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.49,0:19:06.93,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,He really is the type of person \Nyou just can't dislike.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:07.75,0:19:09.71,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,I like you, boy.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.71,0:19:12.32,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,Take care of my granddaughter.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:12.32,0:19:13.13,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I will.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.93,0:19:16.71,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,I'm in a good mood today!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.71,0:19:18.03,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,You there!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:18.45,0:19:20.77,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,Bring out all the booze you've got!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:21.21,0:19:22.72,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,This round's on me!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:23.04,0:19:25.17,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,Everyone who can drink, drink up!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:27.23,0:19:29.72,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Could he be any more extravagant?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.72,0:19:32.85,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,He sure isn't like any \Nof the nobles I know.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.85,0:19:34.23,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,This is yours.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.23,0:19:35.71,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,An engagement gift.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:35.71,0:19:36.88,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,A ring?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.88,0:19:38.14,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,That there is...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:38.51,0:19:40.74,italics,Behemoth,0,0,0,,Show me your strength.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.48,0:19:47.72,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,What is this place?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.37,0:20:00.05,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,"Show me your strength," you say?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.59,0:20:11.93,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Send it flying!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:27.41,0:20:31.87,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\an4\blur2\bord1.5\shad6\fnTimes New Roman\b1\c&HFDFFFD&\3c&HC49676&\4c&H6F3C2B&\pos(284,52.666)}Earth
Dialogue: 0,0:20:27.41,0:20:31.87,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\an4\blur2\bord1.5\shad6\fnTimes New Roman\b1\c&HFDFFFD&\3c&HC49676&\4c&H6F3C2B&\pos(284,117)}Light
Dialogue: 0,0:20:27.41,0:20:31.87,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\an4\blur2\bord1.5\shad6\fnTimes New Roman\b1\c&HFDFFFD&\3c&HC49676&\4c&H6F3C2B&\pos(284,181)}Dark
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.71,0:20:30.36,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,It went up.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:30.36,0:20:31.86,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Light has a +C.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.28,0:20:34.39,italics,Behemoth,0,0,0,,My name is Behemoth.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:35.68,0:20:37.78,italics,Behemoth,0,0,0,,I surrender to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.51,0:20:44.49,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,It's called Behemoth.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:44.49,0:20:46.58,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,Its power pairs with mine.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.58,0:20:47.77,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Like this?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.92,0:21:02.54,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,Even I couldn't win Behemoth over, \Nand you did it in a heartbeat!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.54,0:21:06.11,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Even a man as powerful as Your \NHighness couldn't win it over?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:06.11,0:21:09.07,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,It only told me its name.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:09.07,0:21:14.51,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,I was hoping I'd get to see that \Nfantastical golden figure again.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:14.51,0:21:17.67,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Its figure? Like this?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:20.88,0:21:22.59,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,Yeah! That's it!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:22.59,0:21:26.28,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,You can do that, too?\NYou're really something, boy!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.28,0:21:30.15,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I can learn powers and abilities \Nby making it battle.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:30.15,0:21:32.83,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,Make it battle what?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.83,0:21:34.22,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Well...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.22,0:21:36.94,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I think it'd be faster to just show you.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:39.21,0:21:41.60,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,The magic sword of water, Leviathan.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:42.07,0:21:44.57,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,The ring of flame, Luthier.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:45.04,0:21:47.20,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,The painting of wind, Huwawa.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:48.06,0:21:50.34,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,The ring of earth, Behemoth.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:50.76,0:21:54.04,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,It has been a thousand years \Nsince they were all assembled...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:54.04,0:21:56.50,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,not since the Silver Age.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:56.95,0:21:59.66,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,And the Thirteenth Prince...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:01.34,0:22:05.17,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,Yes, he was about to have \Na wondrous experience
Dialogue: 0,0:22:05.17,0:22:08.24,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,that could only be called a miracle.
